</$objtype/mkfile
APEXPROOT=../../../../..
LIB=$APEXPROOT/$objtype/lib/ape/libedg.a
EDGSRC=../../../external/edg/lib_src

# EDG's OWN C++ runtime -- operator new/delete, vtable support, static
# initialisation, pure-virtual, RTTI -- as C, translated by EDG's own
# C-generating back end.  See sys/src/external/edg/NOTE.
#
# NOT libstdc++ and nothing like it: that is the whole reason this path
# is tractable on a target with no C++ compiler, and it is why this is
# 51 small files rather than a port.
#
# THE ARCHIVE IS WHY THIS GOES FIRST.  The recorded open problem is the
# LINK model -- EDG's COMDAT emulation for vague linkage, with 3,094
# symbols named in more than one of `src''s 75 files -- and an archive
# does not have that problem: `ar' takes duplicate members happily and
# the clash only arrives when something LINKS them.  So this directory
# answers the question nothing has answered yet, "does pcc compile
# EDG's generated C at all", without the link model in the way.
#
# NO -I AND NO -D, deliberately and measured rather than assumed: each
# file here is a WHOLE LOWERED TRANSLATION UNIT and declares everything
# it uses, down to `void *memcpy(void *, const void *, unsigned long
# long)' -- that `unsigned long long' is kencc's own size_t, from
# `kencc_targ.h', so the declarations already describe this target.
# The NOTE records `gcc -fsyntax-only' over all 133 files at 0 errors
# and 0 warnings, which says the sources are clean and says nothing
# about kencc.
#
# CFLAGS is `-c' alone on purpose: every diagnostic is wanted on the
# first run through pcc, and a flag added to quiet one would hide the
# rest.  `-J' arrives from pcc itself and is correct here -- EDG emits
# real `sizeof' expressions rather than the 132 baked-in sizes cfront's
# C carried, so kencc computes every layout and conforming layout is
# exactly what the generated code wants.
#
# THREE OF THESE FILES ARE PREDICTED TO FAIL, and the prediction is
# written here BEFORE the first run so that the result is a measurement
# rather than a discovery.  All three use a feature of the HOST
# compiler rather than anything of EDG's, which is why `gcc
# -fsyntax-only' could never have reported them -- *the host compiler
# is exactly the one that put them there.*  The corpus was swept for
# the whole class at once, with string literals and `#line' stripped
# first (a raw grep counts EDG's own diagnostic text and mangled names:
# `alignof', `typeof', `static_assert' and `_Complex' all appear
# hundreds of times INSIDE identifiers like
# `_ZN3edg27ec_wrong_entity_for_alignasE' and none of them is a
# keyword use).  After stripping, the count of every C11/C23 construct
# kencc lacks is ZERO except these:
#
#	c99_complex.$O	`_Float16', `__bf16', `__float80', `__float128'
#	thread_dtor.$O	`__thread'
#	dtor_list.$O	`__thread'
#
# `c99_complex.c' is the C99 `_Complex' runtime and declares its own
# `struct _Complex_float16 { _Float16 _Vals[2]; }' and so on; the four
# types are gcc's extended floats and kencc has none of them.  The
# other two are thread-local destructor registration for C++ objects
# with static storage, and kencc has no TLS at all.
#
# LEFT IN OFILES DELIBERATELY, not commented out.  With `mk -k' the
# other 48 build and the archive is made from them, and the three
# failures are INFORMATION -- they confirm the sweep named the whole
# class, where removing them first would have made a clean run say
# nothing.  Nothing is known to need them: cpfe is built
# `-fno-exceptions -fno-rtti', is single-threaded, and a C++ front end
# has no use for a `_Complex' runtime -- but *only the link says which
# members are referenced*, so that stays a question until cmd/edg is
# linked.  If it names them, each needs its own answer and neither is
# this mkfile's: extended floats would be a kencc question and TLS a
# libap one.
#
# Two things the same sweep CONFIRMED rather than found, and both are
# about the translation having really used this tree:
# `extern unsigned char _ctype[];' appears in nine of `src''s files,
# byte for byte what APE's own <ctype.h> declares -- so the staged
# headers were APExp's and not glibc's, independently of the NOTE
# saying so.  *It also pins this generated C to this tree's `_ctype'
# BIT LAYOUT*, which the `_ISblank' round changed, so a re-translation
# is the price of changing it again.  And `6c/6.out.h''s `NSYM 50' is
# NOT a cap on symbols per object: `swt.c:229' wraps the slot back to 1
# and re-emits the name, so a 315,616-line translation unit costs
# repeated ANAME records rather than hitting a wall.

OFILES=\
